# Line endings are pinned to LF in the working tree, not just in the repository.
#
# This is load-bearing, not tidiness. The SHA-256 of attack_bank.json is the
# pre-registered instrument fingerprint recorded in PREREGISTRATION.md, and
# verify_all.py checks the shipped file against it. Git's core.autocrlf would
# rewrite that file to CRLF on checkout on Windows, so a fresh clone would
# produce a different hash for a file nobody edited and the project's own
# integrity check would report a violation that did not happen.
#
# Pinning eol=lf makes the checkout byte-identical on every platform, which is
# what "reproducible" has to mean if the fingerprint is going to mean anything.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces on the one file whose exact bytes are pre-registered.
attack_bank.json text eol=lf

# Committed evidence, compared against the numbers quoted in AUDIT.md.
calibration_report.txt text eol=lf
judge_report.txt       text eol=lf

# The web share table is pinned by SHA-256 too (engine.RESOURCE_SHA256).
data/resource_measures.csv text eol=lf
